title Make a look in the font set vtium.conf already uses, at another size and color scheme, use it on no head, and try it: vtium-config says that no head uses the look, and never that the console already uses it.
waits-for CF1 item 1: "already configured" when the look changes what the console shows

# vtium.conf already sets the font set mono for everything.
file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = mono
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf

# The look big: mono, 24 pt, vga, the way the first use case makes it.
press 3 n
press Backspace Backspace Backspace Backspace Backspace Backspace Backspace Backspace
type "big"
press Enter Down Right
press Down Enter End Up Up Enter
press Down Right Right
press Esc
at the look is made
check screen shows "No terminal uses it"
check screen lacks "already"

# t on the look tries it on the console.
press t
at the trial
check screen lacks "already"
press Esc

press s i
at the install question
check screen lacks "already"
press y
at the install
check installed look big font-size 24
check installed look big font-name mono
